From 655de70c39bffb26ce0268bcc66ad1ed233d9db0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:45:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 84/93] test: add p2mr_rescue_tests and the vectors it checks,
 with their generator

The vectors are eight transactions with nine rescue inputs, made once by
test/util/generate_p2mr_rescue_vectors.py with the crate's own prover:
template R1 with the web wallet's K, two inputs in one transaction, |K|
of 1 (the smallest input, whose 130,333-byte witness gives the budget
boundary) and of 64 with suffix 255, OP_CHECKSIGVERIFY, OP_CHECKSIGADD,
a check after OP_CODESEPARATOR, and a leaf with two checks. Their rescue
signature messages come from test_framework/p2mr_rescue.py, an
implementation of its own.

The tests: the parameters of every network, Ark-0 closed at every height
and regtest following the final tripwire height; the block flags at the
height; the token and annex encodings; the key relation; the signature
message against the vectors and every field it commits to; each rule's
failure; the eight combinations of P2MR_TRIPWIRE, P2MR_EC_DISABLED and
P2MR_NO_RESCUE; a 64-byte element starting 03 01 1c checked as Schnorr
through a test hook; the signature cache, counting the proofs the
library verifies (one on a miss, none on a hit, and none when a block
confirms a spend the mempool has checked); the relay template; and, as
tx_valid does but with every prevout in the transaction data, that
taking any restricting flag away from a valid rescue spend keeps it
valid. Rescue spends are not added to tx_valid.json, whose transaction
data has no prevouts.

p2mr_ts_vectors checks the rescue vectors of p2mr-ts, the TypeScript
P2MR library, made independently of this code base and copied into
src/test/data/p2mr_ts_rescue.json (origin and SHA-256 in
p2mr_ts_rescue_vectors.md): the network ids of a custom signet and of
regtest, the five single hashes, the preimage and digest of the rescue
signature message for both inputs on both networks, the key commitment
and m agree byte for byte, and its two-input R1 spend, proved over
regtest's m, verifies at the rescue flags and fails with
SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_NO_RESCUE and on the signet.
